1
00:00:00,996 --> 00:00:03,336
(Mrs Hofstadter:)Would you like for you
and me to talk more?

2
00:00:05,901 --> 00:00:08,351
(Leonard:)You know what? It's probably fine.

3
00:00:08,504 --> 00:00:11,744
(Mrs Hofstadter:)In any event,
while I've had my misgivings

4
00:00:11,907 --> 00:00:14,017
(Mrs Hofstadter:)about... Penny...

5
00:00:15,611 --> 00:00:17,651
(Mrs Hofstadter:)...Sheldon spoke very fondly of her

6
00:00:17,813 --> 00:00:19,653
(Mrs Hofstadter:)and if she is good enough for him,

7
00:00:19,815 --> 00:00:21,855
(Mrs Hofstadter:)then she's good enough for me.

8
00:00:24,586 --> 00:00:28,126
(Leonard:)I'm your son. What about the fact
that she's good enough for me?

9
00:00:30,192 --> 00:00:31,762
(Mrs Hofstadter:)Sure.

10
00:00:33,295 --> 00:00:34,335
(Leonard:)Thanks, Mom.

11
00:00:34,496 --> 00:00:36,336
(Mrs Hofstadter:)Leonard, would it make
you feel better

12
00:00:36,498 --> 00:00:40,608
(Mrs Hofstadter:)to hear that your mother
approved of your life choices?

13
00:00:42,371 --> 00:00:43,611
(Leonard:)Yes, it would.

14
00:00:43,772 --> 00:00:47,122
(Mrs Hofstadter:)Yeah, well, you should work on that.

15
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:55,490
No, Mom, it's the same guy I've gone
out with for the past two years.

16
00:00:55,651 --> 00:00:57,691
(Penny(on phone):)Yeah, the scientist.

17
00:00:57,853 --> 00:01:06,023
(Penny(on phone):)Well, it's complicated. I mean, he
works with lasers and atomic magnets.

